ADAPTATIONS. (1) THE NUMBERS COME IN    1
WITH THE DECK, AS THE DATA LIST L1, NOT 1
BY A READ PROCESS: J182 READS ONLY      1
INTEGERS AND BCD (SECTION 22.0, PAGE    1
236), AND THE LINE READ PROCESSES CAME  1
IN 1964 (SECTION 25.5), AFTER THE FIRST 1
EDITION. (2) THE ELEVEN ARE A LIST, NOT 1
AN ARRAY. J100 AND J64 MAKE A REVERSED  1
COPY, AND J100 GENERATES IT, SO THE     1
ORDER IS A10 TO A0. I IS COUNTED DOWN   1
IN I0 BESIDE IT. (3) THERE IS NO SQUARE 1
ROOT AMONG THE BASIC PROCESSES (SECTION 1
11.0): S1 IS ONE, BY NEWTON'S METHOD.   1
(4) F IS THE ROUTINE F1, WITH ITS INPUT 1
AND OUTPUT IN H0. (5) TOO LARGE IS TWO  1
DATA TERMS, 'TOO L' AND 'ARGE', FIVE    1
CHARACTERS BEING ALL A DATA TERM HOLDS. 1
(6) A NUMBER PRINTS AS J157 ENTERS IT   1
(SECTION 16.2): SIX DIGITS OF FRACTION  1
AND THE EXPONENT, 216246 03 FOR 216.246.1
(7) S1 AND F1 USE W0 TO W2, PRESERVED   1
ON ENTRY AND RESTORED ON EXIT.          1
